# Linux System Check Commands

A single command list for checking CPU, RAM, disk, and network. Run each command manually, or use the all-in-one block at the bottom.

---

## 1. Overview

```bash
hostname
date
uptime
```

## 2. CPU

```bash
nproc
top -bn1 | head -15
top -bn1 | grep "Cpu(s)" | awk '{printf "CPU usage: %.1f%%\n", 100 - $8}'
mpstat -P ALL 1 1
ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head -6
```

## 3. Memory (RAM)

```bash
free -h
free | awk '/Mem/ {printf "Memory used: %.1f%%\n", $3/$2 * 100}'
swapon --show
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head -6
vmstat 1 3
```

## 4. Disk / Volume

```bash
df -h -x tmpfs -x devtmpfs
lsblk
du -sh /var/* 2>/dev/null | sort -rh | head -10
iostat -x 1 3
```

## 5. Network

```bash
ip -br addr
ss -tulpn
ip -s link
ping -c 4 8.8.8.8
dig google.com +short
```

## 6. Interactive Tools

These take over the terminal. Press `q` to quit.

```bash
htop
btop
glances
sudo iotop
sudo nethogs
sudo iftop
```

## 7. Install Optional Tools (Debian/Ubuntu)

```bash
sudo apt install -y sysstat htop btop iotop nethogs iftop dnsutils
```

For RHEL/Fedora, use `sudo dnf install -y sysstat htop iotop nethogs iftop bind-utils`.



Thresholds: 80% CPU, 80% memory, 85% disk. Edit the numbers at the bottom to change them.

